    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1038">

                <pb facs="0798" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 211.52L89.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Spain to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Spanish Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have just received a telegram
                    from the minister of state instructing me to ask of your excellency the
                    provisional detention of Tómas Loscesta and Lazareto Calvo who are to arrive in
                    New York aboard the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Bretagne.</hi></p>
                <p>Proposing to forward to your excellency as soon as they come to hand the papers
                    referring to the offense on which the requisition of His Majesty’s Government is
                    based, I beg your excellency to be so good as to issue as soon as possible the
                    requisite orders for the provisional detention of the said persons on their
                    arrival in New York.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
